     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br>On Friday, June 26, 2015 at 8:04:38 PM UTC+5:30, Phil Chalmers wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Moved this to an issue: <a href=\"https://github.com/philchalmers/mirt/issues/42\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/philchalmers/mirt/issues/42&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792475584269000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2jBjATSGJd2GyAI7W9jh1q\">https://github.com/philchalmers/mirt/issues/42</a>. I&#39;ll take a look when I get a chance. Cheers.<div><br></div><div>Phil</div></div><div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Fri, Jun 26, 2015 at 12:25 AM, Irshad Mujawar <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">irshadmuj...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hello Phil,<br><br>When working with uni-dimensional model if I was giving response pattern for few of the items and make rest in the data as NA I was still getting the fscores() result.<div><br></div><div>When I tried this with 2 dimensional but it is throwing error.</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>I can give an example to demonstrate what is going wrong<br><br><br><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">LSAT7</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>data_LSAT7</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">expand</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">table</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">LSAT7</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><div><br></div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,1